course: dictionary
lesson: 6135
title: One word, three meanings: mil
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Mil» is a short word with more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words and numbers around it. Ask: is this a measurement, an old book, or money talk?
explain: In school problems, mil comes after a number as a unit of thickness. One mil is one thousandth of an inch. Plastic sheets and trash bags are often measured in mils, so «a plastic sheet 4 mils thick» means it is very thin.
explain: In informal talk, «a mil» means a million, often a million dollars. In some old books, mil is a short word for a thousand or a millilitre. Check the context: a money sentence and a thickness sentence need different meanings.
fact: Mil is a noun: one mil, two mils.
fact: One mil is one thousandth of an inch, a unit of thickness.
fact: In some old books, mil can be a short word for a thousand or a millilitre.
fact: In informal talk, «a mil» means a million, as in «a mil dollars».
fact: Spanish uses «mil veces» for «a thousand times», as in «¡Te lo he dicho mil veces!» meaning «I've told you a thousand times!»
exercise: «The plastic sheet is only 4 mils thick.» What does mil mean here? | *A unit of thickness, one thousandth of an inch | A time of day | A kind of bird | A million dollars
exercise: Mia says that in the film, «a mil» means a million dollars. Is she right? | No, mil only ever means a thousand dollars | No, mil is always a unit of weight | *Yes, in informal talk mil can mean a million | No, a mil is a sweet
exercise: In Spanish, «mil veces» means how many times? | *A thousand times | A million times | A hundred times | Once
test: «The bag is 2 mils thick.» What is the best meaning of mil here? | Ten minutes | A kind of sweet | *A unit of thickness | A happy feeling
test: What is the plural of mil? | milli | mile | milles | *mils
exam: In an old recipe book it says «200 mil». What does mil most likely mean? | A plastic bag | A dollar | *A millilitre | A thousandth of an inch
